#
# Counter-example for math:ConditionalIndependenceGivenShape (Rule P9): a
# math:ConditionalIndependenceAssertion that names its subject (math:independenceSubject)
# and the event it is independent of (math:independentOf) but OMITS its conditioning set
# math:independentGiven — the C in A ⫫ B | C — so that property's sh:minCount 1 fires —
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnconditionedAssertion).
# Single violation: math:independenceSubject / math:independentOf carry no SHACL cardinality
# gate, their two ProbabilityEvent targets are not typed logic:Event so
# math:ProbabilityEventOccurrentDisjointShape (P11) stays SATISFIED on them — EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:ConditionalIndependenceAssertion / math:UnconditionedAssertion (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConditionalIndependenceUngivenBad).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:ungivenIndependence a math:ConditionalIndependenceAssertion ;
    math:independenceSubject ex:eventA ;
    math:independentOf ex:eventB .

ex:eventA a math:ProbabilityEvent .
ex:eventB a math:ProbabilityEvent .
